{"title":"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Dr._Xue&#39;s_Math_School\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Dr. Xue's Math School</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In Pascal's Triangle, each entry is the sum of the two entries above it. The first few rows of the triangle are shown below.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0be6c6951f8639445b3d249fd02d722c8be781dc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c@{\\hspace{8em}} c@{\\hspace{6pt}}c@{\\hspace{6pt}}c@{\\hspace{6pt}}c@{\\hspace{4pt}}c@{\\hspace{2pt}} c@{\\hspace{2pt}}c@{\\hspace{2pt}}c@{\\hspace{2pt}}c@{\\hspace{3pt}}c@{\\hspace{6pt}} c@{\\hspace{6pt}}c@{\\hspace{6pt}}c} \\vspace{4pt} \\text{Row 0: } &amp;    &amp;    &amp;     &amp;     &amp;    &amp;    &amp; 1 &amp;     &amp;     &amp;    &amp;    &amp;    &amp;  \\\\\\vspace{4pt} \\text{Row 1: } &amp;    &amp;    &amp;     &amp;     &amp;    &amp; 1 &amp;    &amp; 1  &amp;     &amp;    &amp;    &amp;    &amp;  \\\\\\vspace{4pt} \\text{Row 2: } &amp;    &amp;    &amp;     &amp;     &amp; 1 &amp;    &amp; 2 &amp;     &amp; 1  &amp;    &amp;    &amp;    &amp;  \\\\\\vspace{4pt} \\text{Row 3: } &amp;    &amp;    &amp;     &amp;  1 &amp;    &amp; 3 &amp;    &amp; 3  &amp;     &amp; 1 &amp;    &amp;    &amp;  \\\\\\vspace{4pt} \\text{Row 4: } &amp;    &amp;    &amp; 1  &amp;     &amp; 4 &amp;    &amp; 6 &amp;     &amp; 4  &amp;    &amp; 1 &amp;    &amp;  \\\\\\vspace{4pt} \\text{Row 5: } &amp;    &amp; 1 &amp;     &amp; 5  &amp;    &amp;10&amp;    &amp;10 &amp;     &amp; 5 &amp;    &amp; 1 &amp;  \\\\\\vspace{4pt} \\text{Row 6: } &amp; 1 &amp;    &amp; 6  &amp;     &amp;15&amp;    &amp;20&amp;     &amp;15 &amp;    &amp; 6 &amp;    &amp; 1 \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"437\" height=\"171\" />\nIn which row of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pascal%27s_Triangle\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pascal&#39;s Triangle\">Pascal's Triangle</a> do three consecutive entries occur that are in the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/ceb343fa2c0329c184f390d16f5f3e55358ca534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 :4 :5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider what the ratio means. Since we know that they are consecutive terms, we can say\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3e33483d23203f6389054e0a84815bcffee8cdf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\dbinom{n}{k-1}}{3} = \\frac{\\dbinom{n}{k}}{4} = \\frac{\\dbinom{n}{k+1}}{5}.\\]\" width=\"240\" height=\"74\" />\n</p><p>Taking the first part, and using our expression for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />,\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a578ddb30ed73cbbf73fcd70b6e4feb0840315.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n!}{3(k-1)!(n-k+1)!} = \\frac{n!}{4k!(n-k)!}\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"42\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/3/503bd52bc568692f8226db538887a71a8ccf2b9f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{3(k-1)!(n-k+1)!} = \\frac{1}{4k!(n-k)!}\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"41\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/8/b0848184dfb1eb1b2b3074cfcfa60fcd0e756840.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{3(n-k+1)} = \\frac{1}{4k}\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"41\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/58915a82bb9c25bed309c7fdb8426683e9785266.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n-k+1 = \\frac{4k}{3}\\]\" width=\"119\" height=\"37\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/1/9d1fc2d0b87614a1dacd9bfa2044c68b5ee751a2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = \\frac{7k}{3} - 1\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/4/a14b039f8569191a78cadb9c11599ad92ebdc823.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3(n+1)}{7} = k\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"38\" />\nThen, we can use the second part of the equation.\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b92c7832b5e1fad50b038e35f53521312df40d95.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n!}{4k!(n-k)!} = \\frac{n!}{5(k+1)!(n-k-1)!}\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"42\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/45697a307f8c03fd93bcf6f300ecbec30359f735.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{4k!(n-k)!} = \\frac{1}{5(k+1)!(n-k-1)!}\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"41\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f90a0941474d2a9ddb754d6424e72b98ea2d7c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{4(n-k)} = \\frac{1}{5(k+1)}\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"41\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/9/ac9a70b9c2e531c99cf0232dad21ad5d4469a0b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4(n-k)}{5} = k+1\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/1/051d520344989aa23ee77c2d5df889ac84945b9c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4n}{5}-\\frac{4k}{5} = k+1\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"37\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4aeb3bfc5b1eebc4a99e75d5669f9f898393ac7e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4n}{5} = \\frac{9k}{5} +1.\\]\" width=\"104\" height=\"37\" />\nSince we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/a/5aa192ed01be5886c769478ac877c081f089a59c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\frac{3(n+1)}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"102\" height=\"38\" /> we can plug this in, giving us\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a10463d7114cf38f15cacc7e047b90d09475e56.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4n}{5} = \\frac{9\\left(\\frac{3(n+1)}{7}\\right)}{5} +1\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"52\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/d/e7d539a51583dee03266b1d3c1eba12c5297ad8c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4n = 9\\left(\\frac{3(n+1)}{7}\\right)+5\\]\" width=\"182\" height=\"43\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/b/81b7529b9f6f34b802ceb3c7c0d5137f9fb72818.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7(4n - 5) = 27n+27\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/b/0db774c6a9a001f2d4b994037418f62cceaaa2d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[28n - 35 = 27n+27\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"14\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/6/c46dd6d2b166b7e8df4d68cb0821b5101181d709.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = 62\\]\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />\nWe can also evaluate for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, and find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc7786c31aa51bc842991aa3cc9db29ff1517fb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\frac{3(62+1)}{7} = 27.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" /> Since we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, however, our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b356db957162ae50c68eb804b3b8f675076ad2c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{062.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"23\" /> ~<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/latex.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\LaTeX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> by ciceronii\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call the row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/e/cbe4bb61b58ad07cf526e7ff9f9640691adda4b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=t+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />, and the position of the terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e62900049a5a37a8ef0897449dcf79a21ab3f79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t-1, t, t+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"17\" />. Call the middle term in the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/a/69a140f30bfa5ae88d143f8ca19d1dea4d3f7033.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = \\dbinom{t+k}{t} = \\frac{(t+k)!}{k!t!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"196\" height=\"55\" />. The first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41ec04505eae5098e4c6785aee26df403e2bdd81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\frac{t}{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"64\" height=\"39\" />, and the final term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/748c5bbc0cf28381cba6aa245bd91ad6fb8b7983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\frac{k}{t+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"60\" height=\"41\" />. Because we have the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/c/f5c7e5ac8b9ec338aa09eca12cf8fe6d85eb4b2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3:4:5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb22f7b69128a6800f3abb08c7ea17bb798dd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{t}{k+1} = \\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"84\" height=\"40\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/b/06b18a71060f6a6430859b04946fa70c2af095d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k}{t+1} = \\frac{5}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"81\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55a597a1b6db8b826da93703e35419cb4fbdb883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4t = 3k+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58fb7f98c0eb75a9a0fa93063918707d0b0ad85a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4k= 5t+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e18d59cf925b3e7b1808c3a076ff7994fcee2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4t-3k=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebc097aa802eb7e76a1262b5afb1b06495756e28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5t-4k=-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" /> \n</p><p>Solve the equations to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d14d95fb0a7ce91f4b24b06fd37161709336ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t= 27, k=35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/295fb39dfc770993dc52fdca5d9577b3e059bed2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = t+k = \\boxed{062}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"138\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>-Solution and LaTeX by jackshi2006, variables and algebra simplified by oinava\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Dr._Xue.27s_Math_School\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Dr._Xue's_Math_School\">Video Solution 1 by Dr. Xue's Math School</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Dr. Xue&#39;s Math School\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IG16aQvpEGQ\">https://youtu.be/IG16aQvpEGQ</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME\" title=\"1992 AIME\">1992 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1992 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1992\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183203\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.140 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 287/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1766/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8904/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.631      1 -total\n 59.92%    8.168      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.64%    5.131      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2922:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017183203 and revision id 243845. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}